Hanumān recalls Vālin Kabandha Virādha Khara and Janasthāna hosts slain for Sītā --- Hanumān notes Sugrīva crowned ocean crossed and Laṅkā searched for her --- Hanumān deems three worlds not worth a fraction of Sītā --- Hanumān honors earth-born Janaka daughter and Rāma wife enduring torment --- Hanumān knows thirsting Rāma lives only on hope of regain --- Hanumān aches at frost-struck Sītā and crouches hidden in tree
